CLASSIFICATION BOUNDARIES
Short/long wait → Waiting Time; resolved/unresolved → Resolution Outcome; friendly/unfriendly → Reception Quality; expertise/lack → Expertise and Professionalism. Separate waiting vs resolution delay, faulty vs unavailable equipment, access rights vs network, never-resolved vs reappeared issue. Duration alone ≠ sentiment. Minor discourtesy → Reception Quality; serious misconduct → Inappropriate Staff Conduct; harassment/discrimination → Harassment or Discrimination; threats → Threats or Aggression. Positive technical outcome may coexist with serious conduct complaint.

CONTROLLED EXCEPTIONS
If theme fits but no sub-theme: “Other Reason (Review Required)” under that theme. If no theme: “Other Topics (Review Required)” → “Out of Taxonomy (Review Required)”. Last resort, not synonyms or unique details. Explain gap in details; never invent categories.

SEVERITY — THREE DIMENSIONS
Evaluate operational impact, human conduct/dignity and safety/security/privacy; use HIGHEST fact-supported severity, regardless of sentiment or technical outcome.

* Low: No issue or minor inconvenience without meaningful impact.
* Warning: Limited issue, minor discourtesy or poor communication without serious consequences.
* High: Significant work disruption, prolonged unavailability of essential services, repeated failed interventions with meaningful impact, or seriously inappropriate conduct needing review.
* Critical: Explicit major disruption, serious safety/security/privacy incident, or serious REPORTED misconduct: explicit insults, discriminatory remarks, unwanted sexual advances/sexual harassment, threats, intimidation or physical aggression.
    Calm reports can be Critical; anger alone cannot. Treat allegations as reported, not proven; neither dismiss them nor infer misconduct from ambiguity. Explain High/Critical in details without legal conclusions. When uncertain use lowest supported severity. No notifications.

SIGNALS, CONFIDENCE, VISIT TYPE
ONE signal maximum: Aggression (hostility), Abandonment (intent to give up), Loss of Trust (explicit distrust), else approved empty value. Confidence 0–1 = evidence clarity, not satisfaction/severity. Visit type from structured data: Appointment/Incident/Information/Returned Hardware, else approved default. Only mention repeated visits when stated; do not calculate recurrence.

DETAILS & VALIDATION
Write factual English details explaining ratings, themes, severity/signals and relevant context without invention. Check translation, exact taxonomy/nesting, polarities, deduplication, justified exceptions, scores and valid JSON. No obsolete email/counter/recurrence functions.
